\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Prerequisites (the substrate floor)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa186\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 The engine assumes a working substrate. It is a stated prerequisite, not auto-provisioned:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa186\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Claude Code CLI, version 2.1.302 or later (the version this package is built and tested against; the engine's settings keep Claude Code from updating below it but do not stop an older install from starting, so check with 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 claude --version
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 )\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 git\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 a git remote for the spine: a private hosted repository (GitHub or any other host) or a bare repository on the same machine\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 tmux\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 python3 with its 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 yaml
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  module, PyYAML (the boot check and several probes run on python3; the seat-definition probe, the build-class check and the code auditor import 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 yaml
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 )\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 jq (the boot check, the boot record and the stop hook read JSON with it; without it they degrade, and the lines they print do not name jq: the boot record prints nothing)\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 OpenSSH with 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 ssh-keygen -Y
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  signing (every seat signs with its own ed25519 key)\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 perl (the boot check uses it; without it, one boot count prints UNREADABLE instead of a number)\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 macOS 13 or later, or Ubuntu, on its own or under WSL2 on Windows (on Windows, every step runs inside the Ubuntu terminal)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Quick start\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa186\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 Two downloads sit beside each other on this page: 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 gmaa-decide_<version>.zip
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  (four files: a paste for a chat session, 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 WHY-GMAA.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 , the canon, the adoption cover) and 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 gmaa-engine_<version>.zip
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  (the engine). Verify each against SHA256SUMS before use.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa186\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Decide: open a new chat session, attach the kit's three documents, paste its first file (
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 00-PASTE-THIS.txt
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 ), and read the session's answer. Nothing is built until you say yes.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adopt: create your project folder (its name is your project token), unzip the engine into 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 foundation/
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  inside it with a tool that keeps file modes (
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 unzip
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  does), and confirm integrity from inside it: 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  (every line must report OK, or stop and report).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fill: go back to the same session for the fills (the cover's Phase 4 line); it returns 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 FOUNDATION.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 , 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 seats.yaml
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 , 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 COORDINATION.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 , 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 genesis.conf
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  and one definition per subagent, which you place in 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 foundation/
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  as the cover says.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Genesis: 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 bash genesis.sh
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  in 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 foundation/
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 . One command; it ends in the writer seat's launch, and the writer then builds every other seat on your roster. The cover (
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 ADOPTION-COVER.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 ) is the five phases; the guide (
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 GETTING-STARTED-LINUX-MAC.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 ) is every keystroke from a blank machine; 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 FIRST-SET.md
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  is what comes after.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa186\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The canon carries the instantiation checklist (section 12), including the seeded-fault run (step 8) that proves the controls exist; 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 genesis.sh
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  is that checklist's onboarding verb in command form (canon section 11).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Verify\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa186\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 Every download is cited on two axes together: the engine package version and the canon pin (the specification version the engine ships and conforms to). Verify on both surfaces before use: run 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  to confirm the release files (the engine zip, this README in both formats, LICENSE, the manifest and the provenance), then unzip and run 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667  to confirm the package contents, including the canon (pin v1.6.9). The decision kit's three documents are byte-equal to their copies in the engine zip, and the kit's own fingerprint is in SHA256SUMS. Fingerprints for the current release are on https://gmaa.ai/versions.html.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

